    "failure_scenario": "`run_phase('sidecar_docs', ...)` returns `{escalated: True, reason: 'phase_not_local'}` immediately (line 530–536 of local_llm.py) when the phase is disabled or local LLM is not configured. In that code path the file reads at lines 14–15 and the git subprocess at lines 18–21 all happened for nothing — the prompt is assembled and then discarded. On a large repo with a big SPEC.md and a long diff, this is pure waste on every invocation where local LLM is off. Fix: call `should_use_local('sidecar_docs')` first; if False, write the fallback directly and return."
  },
