    "file": "datum/walkthrough.py",
    "line": 18,
    "summary": "`git diff main..HEAD` subprocess runs unconditionally even when both spec_text and tasks_text are empty strings.",
    "failure_scenario": "If neither SPEC.md nor TASKS.md exists (e.g., the epic directory was just scaffolded), the assembled prompt is `'SPEC:\\n\\nTASKS:\\n\\nDIFF:\\n<full diff>'`. The LLM receives almost no context about the epic but still pays for a potentially large diff read and tokenization. More importantly, the subprocess is also wasted when `run_phase` will fast-exit because the phase is disabled (see candidate 2 above). Fix: guard the subprocess behind the same `should_use_local` early-exit, or at minimum skip it when spec_text and tasks_text are both empty."
  },
